  "prompt": "Use case: precise-object-edit.\nAsset: native1254x1254 opaque daytime city-map continuation r01_c04/s02_02, world [13197,909,14451,2163], core [115,115,1139,1139]. Keep exact framing, scale and camera.\nImage1 is the exact local spatial target, combining just TOP115 rows of valid selected native rear-parapet pixels with an enlarged low-resolution approved-layout guide below. Only those sharp top115 pixels are fixed. The blur below is a geometry guide to newly paint, never to enlarge or sharpen as finished detail. Image2 is the entire4096-world tile's approved layout enlarged ONLY to identify the two parapets and broad horizontal stone wall-top surface; image3 is full-city approved layout only. Images4/5 are actual Daoist chibi hand-painted originals for material finish only; no UI, text or characters.\nCorrect the missed architecture: this is a BROAD, LIGHT STONE HORIZONTAL WALL-TOP WALKWAY seen from above between a rear parapet and a front coping/parapet, NOT one uninterrupted vertical brick wall. At the top, continue the existing back parapet face and small cast shadow naturally out of the native115 strip, roughly to y330 of this crop. Across the middle, roughly y330..850, newly paint the wide sunlit ivory/light-gray stone top plane spanning edge to edge, with very subtle slab joints, fine hand-painted stone shading and restrained foliage shadows. It has real visible depth and must not become stacked front-facing masonry courses.\nAt the near/front edge, around y850 and below, reconstruct the straight horizontal light stone coping/parapet band and the existing SHORT UPRIGHT POST visible near x640 in the guide (approximately topy770, narrow stem descending into coping). It is an architectural stone post with softly rounded/beveled cap, not a freestanding pillar or object on a plaza. Keep its exact guide location and scale. Continue the front face below it and its slim lower cast shadow through the bottom of the crop; the rest continues offscreen into the next southern core. Do not fit the whole wall height into this small image.\nFollow image1's actual faint silhouettes and image2's layer order: rear parapet, broad horizontal pale top plane, near coping with short upright, then front wall/shadow below. Keep the plane broad; do not collapse it to a thin highlight. Existing north endpoints must remain aligned, without an obvious pasted seam at y115. Use existing pale stone hue, gentle daylight, clean rounded hand-painted detail, crisp architectural edges. Avoid photographic roughness, noisy tessellation, honeycomb texture, plastic sheen, blur, new decoration, letters, red plaques, plants, roofs, people, UI or labels. Return one newly painted native1254x1254 crop.",
